{#
Rendered on the target at mode 0600. It carries NO credential -- this is the one
service on the platform whose secrets are all user-owned, and the file is 0600
anyway because every rendered .env here is and a mode that varies by service is
a mode somebody has to justify per service.

ADMIN_TOKEN IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT AND MUST STAY ABSENT. Rendering it empty is
not the same thing: measured against this pin, `ADMIN_TOKEN=` still logs
`[NOTICE] You are using a plain text ADMIN_TOKEN which is insecure` and leaves
the /admin panel reachable, and anything saved there writes a config.json that
outranks every variable in this file from then on. The platform's `${VAR:?}`
convention makes the wrong version easy to reach for, because the obvious way to
render an optional value is to render it empty. tasks/deploy.yml asserts that
neither this template nor the Compose file names it, so adding the line fails
the converge rather than silently disabling the environment.
#}
TZ={{ nas_timezone }}
PLATFORM_CONTAINER_CPUSET={{ platform_effective_container_cpuset }}
PLATFORM_PROJECT_NAME={{ platform_project_name | default('') }}
NAS_UID={{ nas_uid }}
NAS_GID={{ nas_gid }}
VAULTWARDEN_DATA_PATH={{ vaultwarden_data_host_path }}
VAULTWARDEN_HOST_PORT={{ vaultwarden_port }}
VAULTWARDEN_DOMAIN={{ vaultwarden_domain }}
VAULTWARDEN_SIGNUPS_ALLOWED={{ vaultwarden_signups_allowed | bool | lower }}
VAULTWARDEN_INVITATIONS_ALLOWED={{ vaultwarden_invitations_allowed | bool | lower }}
